A design principle for OO inheritance stating that subtypes must preserve behavioral contracts of supertypes, ensuring code using parent class works correctly with any child class - preventing bugs fr

A design principle for OO ${fref("programming-language-theory/concepts/inheritance.td")} stating that subtypes must **preserve behavioral contracts** of supertypes, ensuring code using parent class works correctly with any child class - preventing bugs from unsafe substitution.
